\f1\b \cf4 Production Launch Plan
\f0\b0 \cf2                                                                                                                                                                                   \
                                                                                                                                                                                                          \
  
\f1\b \cf4 \uc0\u55357 \u56628  Critical Blockers (must fix before launch)
\f0\b0 \cf2                                                                                                                                                            \
                                                                                                                                                                                                          \
  ---\
  
\f1\b \cf4 1. YouTube Shorts \'97 Local Filesystem Won't Work in Production
\f0\b0 \cf2                                                                                                                                            \
                                                               \
  Right now clips are saved to \cf5 \cb3 backend/clips_data/\cf2 \cb3  on the local machine. On any cloud host (Vercel, Railway, Render, Fly.io), the filesystem is ephemeral \'97 files disappear on every redeploy.\
                                                                                                                                                                                                          \
  
\f1\b \cf4 Options:
\f0\b0 \cf2 \
  - 
\f1\b \cf4 Cloudinary
\f0\b0 \cf2  (simplest \'97 free 25GB, video support, already has \cf5 \cb3 CLOUDINARY_*\cf2 \cb3  keys in config) \'97 upload the MP4 after yt-dlp clips it, store the Cloudinary URL instead                                    \
  - 
\f1\b \cf4 Cloudflare R2
\f0\b0 \cf2  \'97 cheap (~$0.015/GB), S3-compatible, no egress fees                                                                                                                                     \
  - 
\f1\b \cf4 AWS S3
\f0\b0 \cf2  \'97 industry standard, more setup                           \
  - 
\f1\b \cf4 Persistent volume
\f0\b0 \cf2  on Railway/Render/Fly \'97 if you keep the backend on a single server with a mounted disk, local filesystem actually works fine in prod                                                \
                                                                                                                                                          \
  Recommendation: 
\f1\b \cf4 Use Cloudinary
\f0\b0 \cf2  (it's already half-wired in your config) or 
\f1\b \cf4 Railway with a persistent volume
\f0\b0 \cf2  (zero code changes needed).                                                                 \
                                                                                                                                                                                                          \
  ---                                                                                                                                                                                                     \
  
\f1\b \cf4 2. Supabase RLS is Disabled
\f0\b0 \cf2                                                                                                                                                                              \
                                                                                                                                                                                                          \
  Every user can theoretically read/write every other user's data if they call the DB directly. The service role key bypasses RLS anyway from the backend, but if any key leaks, it's a problem. More\
  importantly, it's not production-grade.                                                                                                                                                                 \
                                                            \
  
\f1\b \cf4 What needs to happen:
\f0\b0 \cf2                                                                                                                                                                                    \
  - Re-enable RLS on \cf5 \cb3 content_items\cf2 \cb3 , \cf5 \cb3 agent_runs\cf2 \cb3 , \cf5 \cb3 notifications\cf2 \cb3 , \cf5 \cb3 connected_accounts\cf2 \cb3 \
  - Add policies: \cf5 \cb3 USING (user_id = auth.uid())\cf2 \cb3  \'97 but since you use Clerk (not Supabase Auth), \cf5 \cb3 auth.uid()\cf2 \cb3  won't match. You have two options:                                                               \
    - 
\f1\b \cf4 Option A (simpler)
\f0\b0 \cf2 : Keep RLS disabled, keep the service role key only on the backend, and rely on your API layer for access control \'97 this is acceptable if the key never touches the frontend\
    - 
\f1\b \cf4 Option B (proper)
\f0\b0 \cf2 : Use JWT claims \'97 configure Supabase to trust Clerk JWTs, then \cf5 \cb3 auth.uid()\cf2 \cb3  will resolve to the Clerk user ID                                                                       \
                                                                                                                                                                                                          \
  Recommendation: 
\f1\b \cf4 Option A for now
\f0\b0 \cf2  \'97 your backend already enforces \cf5 \cb3 user_id\cf2 \cb3  on every query. Add it to the launch backlog.                                                                                  \
                                                                                                                                                                                                          \
  ---                                                                                                                                                                                                     \
  
\f1\b \cf4 3. Change \cf5 \cb3 APP_SECRET_KEY\cf4 \cb3  from Default
\f0\b0 \cf2                                                                                                                                                                    \
                                                            \
  In \cf5 \cb3 config.py\cf2 \cb3 : \cf5 \cb3 APP_SECRET_KEY: str = "dev-secret-change-in-production"\cf2 \cb3  \'97 must be a random secret in prod.\
                                                                                                                                                                                                          \
  ---\
  
\f1\b \cf4 4. Update All CORS Origins
\f0\b0 \cf2                                                                                                                                                                               \
                                                            \
  \cf5 \cb3 CORS_ORIGINS\cf2 \cb3  currently only allows \cf5 \cb3 http://localhost:3000\cf2 \cb3 . Production needs your actual domain: \cf5 \cb3 ["https://yourdomain.com"]\cf2 \cb3 .\
                                                                                                                                                                                                          \
  ---\
  
\f1\b \cf4 5. Switch Clerk to Production Instance
\f0\b0 \cf2                                                                                                                                                                   \
                                                            \
  Clerk has separate dev and production instances. The dev instance has a \cf5 \cb3 localhost\cf2 \cb3 -only JWT issuer. You must create a Clerk production app and get new keys for \cf5 \cb3 NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY\cf2 \cb3 ,\
  \cf5 \cb3 CLERK_SECRET_KEY\cf2 \cb3 , and \cf5 \cb3 CLERK_JWT_ISSUER\cf2 \cb3 .                                                                                                                                                                 \
   \
  ---                                                                                                                                                                                                     \
  
